{
  "id": "noise_generated_by_fans___blade_pass_frequency__bp",
  "title": "Noise generated by Fans - Blade Pass Frequency (BPF)",
  "description": "Calculate the Blade Pass Frequency (BPF) noise generated by a fan based on rotation velocity and number of blades. The BPF varies with the number of blades and rotation speed of the wheel.",
  "type": "calculator-chart",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Blade Pass Frequency (BPF) Calculator\n\nThe Blade Pass Frequency noise generated by a fan can be very intense and varies with the number of blades and the rotation velocity.\n\n### Formula\n\n**BPF = n · t / 60**\n\nWhere:\n- **BPF** = Blade Pass Frequency (Hz)\n- **n** = Rotation velocity (rpm)\n- **t** = Number of blades\n\n### Key Points\n- The energy in the sound may be very high and annoying for the surroundings, especially for fans with few blades\n- The Blade Pass Frequency may not be visible in common fan charts\n- Fan noise in general is documented in octave bands"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "rotation_velocity",
          "label": "Rotation Velocity (n)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "rpm",
          "defaultValue": 2400
        },
        {
          "id": "number_of_blades",
          "label": "Number of Blades (t)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "blades",
          "defaultValue": 10
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "bpf",
          "label": "Blade Pass Frequency (BPF)",
          "formula": "inputs.rotation_velocity * inputs.number_of_blades / 60",
          "unit": "Hz",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
